<title>USA: Lexington B &amp; L Q1 net up on interest gains.</title>
<headline>Lexington B &amp; L Q1 net up on interest gains.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mo. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lexington B &amp; L Financial Corp said Friday net income increased in the first quarter ended December 31 primarily because of an increase in inerest-bearing assets.</p>
<p>The company reported earnings of $205,000 in the period compared with $151,000 one year ago.  Net interest income totaled $559,000 after a provision for loan losses, versus $395,000 in the corresponding period last year, the company said.</p>
<p>Lexington B &amp; L Financial is the parent of B &amp; L Bank.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
